# Help Desk Command Cheat Sheet

## Command Prompt: Networking

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `ipconfig` | Shows the IP address and network info |
| `ipconfig /all` | Shows full details, including MAC address, DNS, and DHCP |
| `ipconfig /release` and `ipconfig /renew` | Drops and requests a new IP address |
| `ipconfig /flushdns` | Clears the DNS cache |
| `ping 8.8.8.8` | Tests connectivity to another device |
| `tracert google.com` | Shows each hop to a destination |
| `nslookup google.com` | Checks DNS resolution |
| `netstat -an` | Lists open connections and listening ports |

## Command Prompt: System and Files

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `hostname` | Shows the computer's name |
| `whoami` | Shows the current user |
| `systeminfo` | Shows OS version, uptime, and hardware info |
| `tasklist` | Lists running processes |
| `taskkill /IM notepad.exe /F` | Force-closes a program |
| `sfc /scannow` | Scans and repairs system files |
| `chkdsk` | Checks the disk for errors |
| `gpupdate /force` | Refreshes Group Policy |
| `gpresult /r` | Shows which policies apply to the user |
| `net user username` | Shows account info and password expiry |

## PowerShell

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `Get-Process` | Lists running processes |
| `Get-Service` | Lists services and their status |
| `Restart-Service -Name Spooler` | Restarts a service (fixes many print issues) |
| `Test-NetConnection google.com -Port 443` | Tests a connection to a specific port |
| `Get-ADUser -Identity username` | Looks up an AD user |
| `Unlock-ADAccount -Identity username` | Unlocks a locked-out account |
| `Get-ADUser -Identity username -Properties LockedOut` | Checks if an account is locked |
| `Get-Help Get-Service` | Shows help for any command |
